                <pb facs="0902" n="818" sameAs="frus:frus1886/pg818"/>

                <head>No. 410.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Curry to Mr. Bayard.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Madrid</hi></placeName>. [<date
                            ana="#date_undated-inferred-from-sibling-dates" calendar="gregorian"
                            notAfter="1886-10-23T14:15:00-05:00"
                            notBefore="1886-10-20T00:00:00-00:14">undated</date>]. (Received October
                        23, 1886.)</dateline></opener>
                <p>Mr. Curry asks to be informed whether Mr. Bayard’s telegram (of 22d) means that
                    he will accept the three propositions offered by the Government of Spain if they
                    are made to include the case of cargoes from foreign countries arriving at the
                    ports of Cuba and Porto Rico in vessels of the United States.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
